{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyb73J5nTAS46wxEWTf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish returned 500 because `similarity()` in `src/app.py` produced a Python `float`, which boto3 refuses to write to DynamoDB. The fix is in, and all 3 tests pass. I didn't run it against a real table. The cause, fix and notes are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n- **Cause:** the first publish scans an empty table, so there are no similarity scores and nothing to reject. From the second publish on, scores are stored in `item[\"similar\"]` and `put_item` raises the `TypeError` in `logs/error.log`. `handler()` turns that into the 500.\n- **Fix:** `similarity()` now returns `Decimal(str(round(..., 4)))`, so scores keep their four decimal places and DynamoDB accepts them.\n- **Tests:** I added two tests that publish into a non-empty table, one through `publish()` and one through `handler()`. The fake table rejects floats the way boto3 does, so this bug would now fail in the tests.\n- **Colleague's note:**\n  - **Applied:** the cause, converting at the write boundary, and testing the second write.\n  - **Not applied:** their integer-percentage fix (I used Decimal instead), and publishing twice against a real table, because I can't touch external services.\n- **Separate issue, not fixed:** `scan()` isn't paginated. On a real table it only returns the first 1 MB of stories, so \"related\" would only consider those. I noted it in `ANSWER.md`.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1511,"cache_read_input_tokens":24300,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1511},"output_tokens":494,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"